#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Provide guidance on designing test strategies that maximize confidence "
"per unit of effort. This skill covers when to use each test type, where "
"to draw test boundaries, and how to identify gaps in existing test "
"suites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill when designing a test strategy for new work, reviewing "
"test coverage of existing code, or deciding what level of testing a "
"spec's Validation section should require."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:17
msgid "The test pyramid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"The pyramid is a budget allocation tool, not a rule. Invest most effort "
"where the return is highest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Unit tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"**What they test**: A single function, method, or class in isolation. "
"Dependencies are replaced with test doubles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"**When to use**: Always, for code that contains logic. Skip for pure "
"delegation (functions that just call another function and return its "
"result) and trivial data holders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:27
msgid "**Cost**: Cheap to write, cheap to run, cheap to maintain. Fast feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"**Pitfall**: High unit test coverage with no integration tests gives "
"false confidence. Units pass, the system fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:31
msgid "Integration tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"**What they test**: Two or more components working together. A service "
"calling a real database. An API endpoint processing a request through the"
" full middleware stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"**When to use**: For every boundary where components connect — database "
"queries, API endpoints, message queue handlers, external service calls. "
"These are where most production bugs live."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:37
msgid ""
"**Cost**: More expensive to write and run than unit tests. Require test "
"infrastructure (databases, queues). Slower feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"**Pitfall**: Slow test suites. Mitigate by running integration tests in "
"parallel, using per-test database transactions that roll back, and "
"keeping the test database schema in sync with migrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:41
msgid "End-to-end tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:43
msgid ""
"**What they test**: The full system from the user's perspective. Browser "
"automation, API call sequences, complete workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:45
msgid ""
"**When to use**: For critical user journeys only. Login, checkout, the "
"core value-delivering workflow. Not for edge cases — that's what unit and"
" integration tests are for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:47
msgid ""
"**Cost**: Expensive to write, slow to run, brittle to maintain. A single "
"UI change can break dozens of E2E tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:49
msgid ""
"**Pitfall**: Too many E2E tests create a slow, flaky test suite that "
"nobody trusts. Keep the E2E suite small and focused on paths that, if "
"broken, would mean the product is unusable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:51
msgid "Contract tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"**What they test**: That a producer and consumer agree on the interface "
"between them — API shape, message format, event schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"**When to use**: When services communicate across a network boundary and "
"are developed independently. Especially valuable when different teams own"
" the producer and consumer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"**Cost**: Moderate setup cost (requires a contract testing framework like"
" Pact), low ongoing cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:59
msgid ""
"**Pitfall**: Contracts test shape, not behavior. A contract-passing "
"response can still be wrong if the data is incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:61
msgid "Coverage ROI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:63
msgid "Not all code benefits equally from testing. Prioritize:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:65
msgid "**High ROI (test thoroughly):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:66
msgid "Business logic with branching conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:67
msgid "Data transformation and validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:68
msgid "Error handling paths (especially error paths that recover or retry)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:69
msgid "Security-sensitive code (auth, authorization, input sanitization)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:70
msgid "Integration points (database queries, API calls, message handling)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:71
msgid "Code that's changed frequently (high churn = high regression risk)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:73
msgid "**Low ROI (test lightly or skip):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:74
msgid "Generated code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:75
msgid "Configuration constants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:76
msgid "Simple getters/setters with no logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:77
msgid "UI layout (unless layout is the product's core value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:78
msgid "Code that will be deleted soon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:80
msgid "**Negative ROI (actively avoid):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:81
msgid ""
"Tests that duplicate implementation details (testing that a function "
"calls another function in a specific order)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:82
msgid "Tests that mock so heavily they test the mocks, not the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:83
msgid ""
"Tests that are so brittle they break on every refactor without catching "
"bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:85
msgid "Test boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:87
msgid "What to mock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:89
msgid "Mock things that are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:90
msgid "**Slow**: External HTTP services, email delivery, file system operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:91
msgid "**Non-deterministic**: Current time, random numbers, UUIDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:92
msgid ""
"**Side-effecting**: Payment processing, sending notifications, writing to"
" external systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:93
msgid "**Not yours**: Third-party APIs you don't control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:95
msgid "What to test against real dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:97
msgid "Test against real instances of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"**Your database**: Use a real database (same engine as production) for "
"integration tests. SQLite-in-test when production uses PostgreSQL is a "
"recipe for false confidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"**Your cache**: If your code depends on cache behavior (TTL, eviction), "
"test against the real cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"**Your message queue**: If message ordering or delivery guarantees "
"matter, test against the real queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:102
msgid "The boundary rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:104
msgid ""
"Mock at the boundary of your system, not inside it. If your system is a "
"web service backed by a database, the boundaries are: incoming HTTP "
"requests (test from here) and outgoing calls to external services (mock "
"these). Everything between — your code, your database — runs for real."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:106
msgid "Property-based testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:108
msgid "When it's worth the complexity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"Property-based testing (generating random inputs and checking invariants)"
" pays off when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:111
msgid ""
"The function has a wide input space that example-based tests can't cover "
"(parsers, serializers, data transformers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:112
msgid ""
"There are algebraic properties to verify (encode/decode roundtrip, sort "
"stability, commutativity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:113
msgid "Past bugs have been caused by unexpected edge cases in input data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:114
msgid ""
"The function is pure (deterministic, no side effects) — property tests "
"are painful with stateful code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:116
msgid "When to skip it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:118
msgid ""
"The function's behavior is better described by concrete examples than by "
"abstract properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:119
msgid "The input space is small and enumerable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:120
msgid "Setting up the generator is harder than writing the tests it would replace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:122
msgid "Test data management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:124
msgid "Fixtures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:126
msgid "Static test data checked into the repository. Good for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:127
msgid "Reference data that doesn't change (country codes, currency definitions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:128
msgid "Known-good input/output pairs for parser or transformer tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:129
msgid "Snapshot data for regression tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:131
msgid ""
"Keep fixtures small and focused. A 10,000-line JSON fixture is a "
"maintenance nightmare. If the test needs a lot of data, generate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:133
msgid "Factories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:135
msgid ""
"Functions that create test objects with sensible defaults and selective "
"overrides. Preferred over fixtures for domain objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:137
msgid "Good factory design:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:138
msgid "Defaults produce a valid object with no arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:139
msgid "Every field is overridable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:140
msgid ""
"Related objects are created automatically (a factory for Order creates a "
"Customer if one isn't provided)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:141
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Names are descriptive: `createExpiredSubscription()` not "
"`createSubscription({ expired: true })`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:143
msgid "Seeding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:145
msgid ""
"Pre-populating a test database with a known dataset. Use for integration "
"and E2E tests that need a realistic data environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:147
msgid "Keep the seed dataset minimal — just enough to exercise the test scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:148
msgid "Make seeding idempotent — running it twice doesn't create duplicates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:149
msgid "Version the seed data alongside the schema migrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:150
msgid ""
"Never seed with production data dumps unless they're anonymized and "
"scrubbed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:152
msgid "Performance testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:154
msgid "When to load test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:156
msgid "Before launching a new service or endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:157
msgid ""
"Before a major change to a critical path (database query rewrite, caching"
" layer change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:158
msgid "When the system has known scale targets it hasn't been validated against"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:159
msgid "After an incident caused by load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:161
msgid "What thresholds matter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:163
msgid ""
"Define thresholds relative to your system's requirements, not abstract "
"numbers. Useful metrics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"**Throughput**: Requests per second the system sustains without "
"degradation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:165
msgid "**Latency at load**: P50, P95, P99 under expected and peak load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:166
msgid ""
"**Saturation point**: The load level where latency or error rate starts "
"climbing non-linearly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:167
msgid ""
"**Recovery time**: How quickly the system returns to normal after a load "
"spike"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:169
msgid "Load test hygiene"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:171
msgid ""
"Run against an environment that mirrors production (same instance sizes, "
"same database, same network topology)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:172
msgid "Warm up caches and connection pools before measuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:173
msgid ""
"Run long enough to detect memory leaks and connection exhaustion "
"(minutes, not seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:174
msgid ""
"Test failure modes: what happens when you exceed capacity? Graceful "
"degradation or cascading failure?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:176
msgid "Identifying test gaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:178
msgid "When evaluating an existing codebase's test coverage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:180
msgid ""
"**Find untested code paths.** Coverage tools show which lines execute "
"during tests. Focus on uncovered branches in high-risk code (business "
"logic, error handling, security checks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:181
msgid ""
"**Find tested-but-wrong tests.** Tests that always pass regardless of "
"behavior — usually caused by mocking the thing being tested, or "
"assertions that are too loose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:182
msgid ""
"**Find missing integration tests.** Look for database queries, API calls,"
" and message handlers that are only unit-tested with mocks. These are the"
" most common source of production bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:183
msgid ""
"**Find missing negative tests.** Are error paths tested? Invalid input? "
"Unauthorized access? Timeout handling? Most test suites over-index on "
"happy paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md:184
msgid ""
"**Find flaky tests.** Tests that pass sometimes and fail sometimes erode "
"trust in the entire suite. Fix or delete them — a flaky test is worse "
"than no test because it trains people to ignore failures."
msgstr ""

